when do you expect your banking  relationships to be restored well I hope  as soon as possible die  you know we've got 7500 staff members  and the immediate families which I would  estimate to be about 60,000 people  really worried about their futures I  listen to some of them calling in local  radio stations over the weekend  imploring the banks do to do to step up  to the plate and resume normal relations  with ourselves I hope that I can get  some appointments with the bank's this  morning and convince them to the to  restore our relations are you talking to  the same institutions that have walked  away from you are you talking to new  possible financial institutions that  could work with you give us some names  here who has walked away from you and  who do you expect to be re-establishing  relationships with or establishing  relationships with well in the South  African context therefore major banks  all four have walked away from us we  need one of them at least to offer some  kind of services so we'll be talking to  all four banks again this week and  assuring them of our governance being in  place the correctness of what we've done  and and really we can implore them to  think about our workers that's the 7,500  in the immediate families that is really  what matters today is that their  livelihoods are not affected by this  decision you confirmed last week that  you had contacted various government  officials to try and assist you in  reestablishing these relationships I'm  really curious about this why did you  think that that was a good course of  action given the fact that it's this  political business link that seems to be  at the heart of this story and what kind  of reaction did you get when you  contacted those officials well you know  let me start off why did we do it very  simply to save jobs South Africa's major  challenge today is jobs and job creation  and were 7,500 jobs at risk it was do  whatever it takes to get that going  that was the only reason for writing to  the institution's the Minister of  Finance is politically responsible for  the banking sector and it's  unprecedented for for banking  institutions the four major banking  institutions to all walk away from a  business it's never happened in this  country it's never happened I think in  the world that the major banking  institutions would do something like  this  so it was really to plea for or for some  kind of assistance and guidance on how  we can try and restore those  relationships no other reason that we  would do that  what responsive we've had very little  right now from those incident from that  little leadership but we will continue  to do whatever it takes will speak to  whatever it we can business  organizations political organizations  the banks themselves community  organizations to to really plea for the  jobs of our people mr. hower Hots  Nichols here in Berlin you say you're  gonna be reaching out to those four  banks how much time are you giving  yourself to restore relations is there  is there any sort of time limit here are  we talking days or weeks well the banks  have given us until the end of May so  we've we've got a couple of weeks to get  to get either the relationships restored  or caught under the plan but you know  without the four major banks we very  clear in our heads that the jobs are at  risk and in fact I think you know with  one of our businesses we may need to  take some drastic measures this week was  that business works with all four banks  and its revenues will be infected  immediately that the banking services  are overthrown so there we may need to  take some some very serious and drastic  steps this week already of one of our  businesses what is what is all about  this is you've already highlighted as is  four major banks walking away from a  company on mass that strikes you I'm  sure as odd that strikes me I think as  odd what do you think sparked this was  there coordination between these banks  was there pressure put on them by  somebody else the third party for them  to walk away to the new piece of  information become available why did it  happen so suddenly and with all four  major banks being involved at the same  time well I you know I want in two ways  I got asked by one of the editors of one  of the major financial institutions  whether we believe there's a third force  at end we don't have any concrete  evidence of that so I I don't want to  make that assumption that what sumption  was made by the editor financial mail  but you know clearly as I say it's  unprecedented it's never happened before  and you know particularly in a country  where we've had major  and scandals where the bends have never  taken those tips against any other  business we the first business had  suffered this kind of action but the  second point I would make to you is that  what surprises us is this this very  strong action is taken against a  backdrop of not a single charge being  laid against us no evidence of any  corruption or anything else and you know  South Africa prides itself on having a  once wonderful Constitution which  presumes you innocent until proven  guilty it would seem that our 7500 staff  members and if they lively which they've  taken away must be able to say that  we've been punished for something we've  not done anything about we've not been  guilty of anything but 7,500 people are  likely to lose their jobs because of  this decision taken for reasons best  known to the banks not to ourselves so  mr. Howe how will you will you go to the  bank so you meet with them in the coming  days is your argument about the job  losses or are you gonna be making a  fundamentally different argument to them  how are you gonna convince them to  restore relations I really will start  with the job losses because that's the  most important thing to me we like a  family of the 7,500 staff or our family  for them and the immediate families to  be impacted by this decision is really  something that we want to avoid at all  costs my first plea will be around the  issue of job losses my second argument  will be around the issue of we're making  decisions against a backdrop of no  concrete evidence or no concrete finding  these events anyone in the group anybody  in the shielding structure anything else  and that surely if we believe in the  constitutional democracy we all talk  about sobra so broadly we must assume  innocent until proven guilty and not  simply moving and and really create a  stranglehold around our business to  force us out of business and to lose  these 7,500 jobs just to follow up on  that point though what it's the guptas  relationship with the business that  obviously is causing the financial  institutions their concern and their  concern surrounding the political  scandal do you think that the action  taken thus far by your shareholder is  enough to convince the banks or do you  think that actually you will you guys  are going to need to talk about maybe  your shareholder divesting the stake in  the business  well I think that's not a decision for  me to take that's a shell the decision  on whether I want to divest or not and  there's no indication at this point that  they want to do that but I think you  know from our point of view I think the  shelters have taken what I think is a  big sacrifice they've made a big  sacrifice to save the 7,500 jobs and I  would argue that that should be enough  for the banks who do the right thing to  save these jobs right now okay have you  spoken to the shareholder over the last  what have you spoken to the shareholder  since Friday he's spoken to the Gupta  since Friday no I've not I've no up not  they've taken the decision to to  distance himself from the business and  they've lived up to that decision and  they've left us as the management team  to take charge of the business on a  day-to-day basis do you if you need to  talk to them do you know where they are  certainly I know where they are they've  not in hiding they've not fled the  country so I certainly I know where they  are but the decision they've taken is  that the management will run the  business and they've entrusted us with  every single decision

